# MASTER PROJECT PROMPT
# AUTOMOTIVE WIRING HARNESS WORK STUDY, STANDARD WORK & MANPOWER PLANNING SYSTEM

**Project Name:** Automotive Work Study & Manpower Planning System (AWSMPS)  
**Version:** 1.0  
**Application Type:** Local Web Application  
**Technology:** PHP 8+, MySQL/MariaDB, HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, Bootstrap 5  
**Deployment:** Windows PC with XAMPP, Apache, and MariaDB/MySQL  
**Network:** Internal plant LAN; internet connection must not be required  
**Final Deliverable:** Complete, runnable application packaged as a ZIP file

---

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Develop a complete web-based system for managing work study, workload distribution, standard work documentation, operator training preparation, and manpower planning for automotive wiring harness assembly production.

The system will be used by a team of skilled manpower responsible for studying new products, analyzing production processes, determining the correct work content, creating workloads, documenting standardized work procedures, and transferring the studied work to mass production operators.

The system must convert the team's existing video-recording-based work-study method into a structured, measurable, traceable, and repeatable digital process.

The ultimate objective is to determine:

1. What work must be performed for each automotive wiring harness product model.
2. How each operation must be performed correctly according to established standards.
3. How much time each operation requires.
4. How operations should be grouped and distributed among operators.
5. How many operators are required based on order quantity, available production time, and target cycle time.
6. Whether the proposed workloads are balanced and achievable.
7. Whether the documented standard work has been transferred successfully to mass production.
8. Whether actual production performance confirms the original work-study assumptions.

The application must serve as a **work-study engineering tool, standard work management system, workload balancing tool, and manpower planning system**.

It must not be merely a static dashboard or a basic data-entry application.

