## 2. CORE SYSTEM PRINCIPLE

The system must maintain a traceable connection between:

**Product Model → Product Configuration → Work Study → Video Analysis → Operation Time → Standard Work → Workload Distribution → Manpower Calculation → Training Transfer → Mass Production Verification → Continuous Improvement**

Every production model must have its own controlled work-study records and standard work documentation.

Do not assume that different housing types, product models, circuit configurations, or wiring harness variants share the same work content.

Changes in product design, circuit quantity, housing, components, process sequence, or work method must trigger a review of the affected work-study records.

The system must preserve historical approved standards and must not silently overwrite previously approved work studies.

