- Downtime.
- Quality defects.
- Rework.
- Operator training status.
- Work-method deviations.
- Material shortages.
- Equipment constraints.
- Actual workload observations.
- Supervisor remarks.

Compare planned and actual results.

Calculate:

Output achievement = Actual output ÷ Planned output × 100%.

Cycle-time gap = Actual cycle time − Target cycle time.

Manpower gap = Actual manpower − Approved planned manpower.

Show positive and negative gaps with clearly defined interpretation.

Identify whether poor performance is associated with work content, manpower shortage, operator skill, equipment, materials, quality issues, or other documented factors.

Do not automatically assign blame to operators without evidence.

Allow the engineer to initiate a new work study or improvement project when actual results differ materially from the approved plan.

