## 8. DATA VALIDATION AND BUSINESS RULES

Apply these rules throughout the application:

1. No approved standard time without traceable observations or an explicitly documented alternative approved method.
2. No approved manpower plan without a defined production demand, target cycle time, net available time, and documented assumptions.
3. No assignment to a nonexistent product, revision, process, workstation, or task.
4. No negative time values.
5. No duplicate workload assignment unless the task model explicitly permits it.
6. No silent modification of approved records.
7. No approval by an unauthorized user.
8. No automatic replacement of a valid approved standard when a new study is created.
9. No misleading presentation of theoretical capacity as actual output.
10. No unverified constraint marked as passed.
11. No unsupported claim of AI automation.
12. No deletion of audit history through ordinary user actions.

Allow approved exceptions with reasons and responsible approvers.

All calculations must have documented units and explicit rounding rules.

Use decimal or sufficiently precise numeric storage for time and calculations. Apply rounding only for presentation or at explicitly defined business-rule boundaries.

